    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360-a1">

                <pb facs="0441" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg269"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Minister of Guatemala, Washington</hi>: Replying
                    to your cablegram of yesterday, it affords me pleasure to say to you that
                    without any prompting and in the most spontaneous manner all that you suggest in
                    your cablegram is done. All that is wanting is that you ask of the Department of
                    State of the United States that in communications made to you there and to
                    Minister Lea veil here at the same time, it be pleased to tell us that it
                    accepts and agrees to our participation and what are the terms of defensive
                    alliance. I understand, as I already said to you in a letter, that an exchange
                    of notes of receipt will suffice for this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel Estrada Cabrera</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
